---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "APR for Student Loans (What to compare)";
const description =
  "Compare student loan APRs by aligning term, fees, and repayment plan. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-02-17";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/student-loan-apr-comparison" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Student loan APR</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Student loan APR comparison</h1>
    <p>
      Student loans can have different terms and repayment plans. This guide shows how to compare APR and total cost
      with consistent assumptions.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-comparison-checklist">APR comparison checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">APR comparison inputs to verify</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan amount and term (keep them constant across offers).</li>
      <li>Nominal rate vs APR and which fees are included.</li>
      <li>Upfront fees paid in cash vs financed.</li>
      <li>Expected time horizon before refinance or payoff.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What to align</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Same loan amount and term.</li>
      <li>Same fee treatment and repayment plan.</li>
      <li>Same time horizon if you plan to prepay.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Comparing fixed and variable APRs without a horizon.</li>
      <li>Ignoring origination fees or capitalized interest.</li>
      <li>Comparing offers with different repayment plans.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Repayment plan impact</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Income-driven plans can change the effective cost over time. If you expect to switch plans, compare APR and total cost over the
      same expected horizon rather than the full term.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Federal vs private notes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Federal loans may include protections that affect total cost risk.</li>
      <li>Private loans often price based on credit and can vary by term.</li>
      <li>Compare on the same repayment plan and horizon before deciding.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision inputs</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Expected repayment plan over the next few years.</li>
      <li>Any income changes that could shift plan eligibility.</li>
      <li>Grace period length and capitalization rules.</li>
      <li>Subsidized interest coverage, if applicable.</li>
      <li>Planned payoff horizon or refinance timing.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare federal vs private terms on the same horizon.</li>
      <li>Model payments under the plan you expect to use.</li>
      <li>Include any interest capitalization events.</li>
      <li>Test an early payoff or refinance scenario.</li>
      <li>Compare total dollars paid across scenarios.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Documents to compare</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Loan disclosure with fees and capitalization rules.</li>
      <li>Rate type details (fixed vs variable) and reset timing.</li>
      <li>Repayment plan schedule and required minimums.</li>
      <li>Any grace period terms or deferment policies.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/apr-comparison-checklist">APR and prepayment</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/personal-loan-apr-comparison">Personal loan APR comparison</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Do federal loans include fees in APR?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Federal loan terms vary by program. Review the disclosure to understand how fees are treated.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I compare total dollars paid?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes. APR is useful, but total dollars paid over your horizon is the final comparison.
    </p>
  </section>

    <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">References</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/ask-cfpb/what-is-apr-and-why-is-it-higher-than-my-interest-rate-en-156/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          What is APR and why is it higher than my interest rate?
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        CFPB:{" "}
        <a href="https://www.consumerfinance.gov/paying-for-college/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Paying for college (student loan basics)
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

<section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/apr-calculator">Compare APR offers</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/apr-comparison-checklist">APR checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/apr">APR topic</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-02-08</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>





